R-SO19 R-SO22 R-SO23 R-SO24 R-SO14 R-SO15 R-RP3 R-BL6 R-H6 R-DL2 R-DL5 R-LF1 R-SP21 R-P5 R-PP4 R-EC18 (slice 072e, Q-D2 of slice 072d, Q-E1): the commands of the install family with checks, no `roc:` pin and no compiler selected. By R-SO24 this means that nothing is installed (no `roc` on `PATH`, no `default-roc`, no `ROC_TOOLCHAIN`). The compiler is picked before the index and before any write, as an id (R-SO19, R-SO23): the newest compiler in the channel with a recorded pass for each header hash that has a fact, else the latest in the channel. The download, when the id is not installed, is the first probe (R-SO22), and the downloaded compiler becomes `default-roc` (R-SO24). The pin is written after the check passes (R-RP3). 7 runs, each on its own home (h1 to h7) and project (n1 to n7, the header of `verify/vn1-nocompiler`). `update json` moves json 2.1.0 to 2.2.0.
Run 1 (h1, no fact, `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=yes`): nothing is installed, no fact. The pick is the latest in the channel (N4). The calls show the order: the list and the facts of the pick, the index of `acme/json`, then the download at the first probe (the line `downloading <id> (<size>), the default compiler`), the write of `default-roc` in `config.toml`, the probes. The header gets `+ roc: N4`.
Run 2 (h2): nothing is installed, `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=no`: exit 13 at the first probe (R-DL5), after the index. The project file is not written, no download, no default.
Run 3 (h3, `--no-check`): nothing is installed. No probe runs, so the run picks nothing (R-SO19, R-BL6): no list of compilers, no download, no default, `check: skipped`, json moves, no `roc:` pin (R-H6).
Run 4 (h4, `remove json`, `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=yes`): nothing is installed. `remove` with checks picks and downloads at its first probe, as run 1: the entry is removed and `+ roc: N4`.
Run 5 (h5, `install --frozen`, with a `talon.toml`): nothing is installed. `--frozen` runs no probe, so it picks nothing (R-SO19, R-SO22): no list of compilers, no download, no default. The packages of the header are in the cache (no unbundle): `the header satisfies talon.toml`, exit 0.
Run 6 (h6, facts, `TALON_AUTO_INSTALL=yes`): nothing is installed. The facts say pass for the 3 header hashes on N1 and N2. The pick is N2, the newest with a pass, and not the latest N4. N2 downloads at the first probe, becomes `default-roc`, and the header gets `+ roc: N2`.
Run 7 (h7, Q-E1 (a), plain `install` with a `talon.toml`): nothing is installed. The header satisfies `talon.toml` (the pure check of `--frozen`, R-LF1), so the plain `install` has nothing to change: it picks nothing and needs no compiler (R-SO19). No list of compilers, no download, no default.
The pick of `tln install` with no `talon.toml` is in `resolve/rs-no-compiler` run 1 and `roc/so9-no-roc`. Runs with compilers installed and no `default-roc` are not here: R-SO24 case 3 is slice 080.
